@startuml <SLUG>_IBD
' =====================================================================
' Internal Block Diagram (IBD) — STARTER TEMPLATE  (Phase 03, diagram 3 of 7)
' Rename file to IBD_<TopBlock>.puml for the actual top block.
' Builds on: the most critical block from the BDD (usually the controller / service mesh).
' Conventions §7. Replace <PLACEHOLDERS>; delete (example) lines.
' Ports:  standard ports = interface-based interactions (service/operation calls)
'         flow ports     = material / energy / data exchange (signal/data/physical flow)
' The ports here imply the ICD seams frozen in Phase 04.
' =====================================================================
title <Top Block> — Internal Block Diagram (TODO)

component "<Top Block>" as TopBlock <<block>> {
  component "<Internal Part 1>" as Part1 <<part>>
  component "<Internal Part 2>" as Part2 <<part>>
  component "<Internal Part 3>" as Part3 <<part>>
  ' component "Comms Module" as Part1 <<part>>   ' (example — delete)

  ' --- Ports on the boundary ---
  portin  "<stdPort: service in>"  as PstdIn
  portout "<flowPort: data out>"   as PflowOut
}

' --- Internal flows between parts (signal / data / physical) ---
Part1 --> Part2 : <flow: data/signal>
Part2 --> Part3 : <flow: data/signal>

' --- Boundary ports wired to internal parts ---
PstdIn  --> Part1 : <<standard port>> <service call>
Part3   --> PflowOut : <<flow port>> <data/energy>

note bottom of TopBlock
  TODO: each boundary port becomes an ICD-<nn> seam in Phase 04.
  satisfies REQ-INT-<nn> / REQ-<id>
end note

@enduml
